course: dictionary
lesson: 3167
title: Understanding feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Empathy is a word for understanding how someone else feels. Its meaning is «imagining how someone else feels», as if you were standing in their place. People also say «walking in their shoes».
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Grown-ups feel sad when they see people suffering, even far away; this is empathy.» The sadness is about people you may never meet, so empathy can reach people who are far away. Ask yourself: how would I feel if that happened to me?
explain: Empathy helps you choose kindness. «Kindness is choosing to help, include and care, and it grows from empathy.» Before you act, think about how the other person feels. That thought is what makes your help kind.
fact: Empathy means understanding and sharing the feelings of another person.
fact: «Show empathy» and «have empathy for» are common phrases.
fact: «Put yourself in someone's shoes» means imagining being in another person's place.
fact: Feeling with someone is different from feeling for them: empathy is about understanding how they feel.
fact: «Inclusion» means making sure people are not left out, and empathy helps us do this.
exercise: Mia noticed Sam was quiet at lunch and imagined how lonely he might feel. What does Mia show? | *Empathy | Boredom | Hunger | Anger
exercise: What does empathy mean? | Winning every game | *Understanding and sharing how someone else feels | Being very loud | Forgetting what people say
exercise: «Put yourself in someone's shoes» means | Take their things | Walk faster than everyone else | *Imagine being in their place | Buy new shoes for a friend
test: What does «have empathy for» suggest? | You want to argue with them | *You understand how they feel | You dislike them | You have never met them
test: Which phrase means imagining how someone else feels? | Buying new shoes | *Walking in their shoes | Shoes on the table | Walking away from the park
exam: Which choice best shows empathy? | Sam laughed at his friend's dropped lunch | Sam ran off to tell everyone | *Sam saw his friend had dropped her lunch and helped her pick it up, thinking how upset she must feel | Sam ignored the mess and went outside
